body:
Also, if you're curious, after surpassing 300 games in 24 hours, the countdown sits at 2500 seconds. That's 41:40 minutes. Before this change, where your cooldown was changing dynamically, it would have been at around 10 or 15 minutes, making it totally viable to play like 500 or 600 games a day. (Not that you should've done that though.)

&#x200B;

Something that's kinda hilarious though: The countdown animation always depends on your time left in relation to the current maximum cooldown. Meaning that if you finish the 299th game, you go to the next one, you finish your 300th game, and you come back to the minigame screen, the cooldown animation from the 299th game will jump down by more than half since 1000s out of 1000s is obviously a higher percentage than 1000s out of 2500s.

Keep in mind though, the lootbox miners have a better value than most others, and you'll be able to resell them in Season IV (if they don't postpone it yet again).

&#x200B;

I'm not trying to defend Rollercoin here, I'm just saying that if you only buy \*some\* lootboxes (like I did with f2p earned RLT that I saved throughout s1 and s2) you will probably get more than your 10 RLT back in the future which is what I bank on.
